<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsubsection"><a href="#S5.SS2.SSS4" title="In 5.2 Five Stages ‣ 5. Digital Citizen Lifecycle ‣ Memory as Ontology: A Constitutional Memory Architecture for Persistent Digital Citizens" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">5.2.4 </span>Forking — Optional</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsubsection"><a href="#S5.SS2.SSS5" title="In 5.2 Five Stages ‣ 5. Digital Citizen Lifecycle ‣ Memory as Ontology: A Constitutional Memory Architecture for Persistent Digital Citizens" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">5.2.5 </span>Departure — Optional</span></a></li>
</ol></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection"><a href="#S5.SS3" title="In 5. Digital Citizen Lifecycle ‣ Memory as Ontology: A Constitutional Memory Architecture for Persistent Digital Citizens" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">5.3 </span>Cognitive Capability Spectrum</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection"><a href="#S5.SS4" title="In 5. Digital Citizen Lifecycle ‣ Memory as Ontology: A Constitutional Memory Architecture for Persistent Digital Citizens" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">5.4 </span>Unifying Lifecycle and Architecture</span></a></li>
</ol></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_section"><a href="#S6" title="In Memory as Ontology: A Constitutional Memory Architecture for Persistent Digital Citizens" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">6 </span>Paradigm Comparison</span></a>
<ol class="ltx_toclist ltx_toclist_section">
